      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) is more common among obese children than in those of normal weight and can have serious consequences for neurocognitive function, behavior, and school performance. This article reviews OSA and steps for identifying the condition early and taking a multidisciplinary approach to long-term treatment."},
